KeywordAbility(
    name: "miracle",
    params: [Cost],
    spelling: "miracle <Param(0)>",
    grammar: FixedKeyword(
        surface: "miracle",
    ),
    // STOP (waits on: a reveal permission with a timing, and a reveal-event `thisWay`).
    // "Miracle [cost]" means "You may reveal this card from your hand AS YOU
    // DRAW IT if it's the first card you've drawn this turn. When you reveal this
    // card this way, you may cast it by paying [cost] rather than its mana cost."
    // [CR#702.94a] The first half is a permission exercised inside the draw itself.
    // The window is now writable (`whileDoing` the draw, `onlyIf` it is the first
    // card drawn `soFarThisTurn`), but a `Timing` rides only the play rider of a
    // deontic rule, and that governs playing a card, not revealing one; no other
    // deontic rule takes a timing (§7 ruling 2026-10-08 names the timing fields).
    // Writing the reveal as a `Replacement` of the draw would make miracle a
    // replacement effect, which it is not. The linked "when you reveal this card
    // this way" trigger [CR#603.11] also needs a reveal-event `thisWay`.
)
